        "3": "The function number, 9 for Cconws, takes 2 more bytes on the stack.",
        "4": "\`TRAP #1\` calls the GEMDOS, which reads the number and the parameter from the stack and displays the text up to its final 0.",
        "5": "The program cleans 4 + 2 = 6 bytes off the stack, and SP returns to its starting value.",
        "6": "The pushed 0 selects the Pterm0 function.",
        "7": "The GEMDOS ends the program and hands control back to the GEM desktop, without returning."
