      "explications": {
        "2": "The 68000 handled \`$A000\` as an exception, and TOS returned in A0 the address of the Line A variables, \`$0E80\` in the simulator.",
        "3": "A5 keeps that address, which the following calls could wipe out of A0.",
        "5": "The first word of INTIN receives the color of the pixel, 1.",
        "8": "PTSIN now holds the coordinates, x = 160 then y = 100.",
        "9": "\`$A001\` sets the pixel (160, 100) in color 1, a red dot in the middle of the screen.",
        "13": "Color 3 is written \`%0011\`, and only planes 0 and 1 receive a 1.",
        "14": "The pattern \`$FFFF\` gives a solid line.",
        "15": "Mode 0, replace, draws the color where the pattern is 1.",
        "19": "The ends are in place, from (10, 10) to (300, 190).",
        "20": "\`$A003\` draws the diagonal in color 3, which passes very close to the red dot."
      },
